<GuideLayout
  title="Debian Distribution"
  description="Step-by-step guide to building a custom Linux distribution based on Debian. Covers debootstrap, package management, branding, and generating a bootable ISO image."
  difficulty="Intermediate"
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="introduction">
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      Building your own Linux distribution lets you create an operating system tailored to your
      exact needs. Debian is an excellent base: proven stability, over 50,000 packages, strict
      quality control, and a large community.
    </p>
    <Note>
      <strong>Note:</strong> This guide assumes basic familiarity with Linux and the command line.
    </Note>

    <h3>Why Debian as a base?</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Years of proven stability and reliability</li>
      <li>Massive package repository (50,000+ packages)</li>
      <li>Rigorous quality control process</li>
      <li>Excellent documentation and active community</li>
      <li>Flexible configuration and adaptation</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="preparation">
    <h2>Preparation</h2>

    <h3>System requirements</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>A Linux machine (Debian or Ubuntu preferred)</li>
      <li>4 GB RAM minimum (8 GB recommended)</li>
      <li>20 GB free disk space</li>
      <li>Stable internet connection</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Install required tools</h3>

    <h4>Debian / Ubuntu</h4>
    <pre><code>sudo apt update
sudo apt install debootstrap squashfs-tools xorriso isolinux \
  syslinux-common grub-pc-bin grub-efi-amd64-bin mtools \
  live-build cdebootstrap</code></pre>

    <h4>Fedora</h4>
    <pre><code>sudo dnf update
sudo dnf install debootstrap squashfs-tools xorriso syslinux \
  grub2 mtools genisoimage</code></pre>

    <h4>Arch Linux</h4>
    <pre><code>sudo pacman -Syu
sudo pacman -S debootstrap squashfs-tools libisoburn syslinux grub mtools</code></pre>

    <h3>Create the working directory</h3>
    <pre><code>mkdir -p ~/mydistro/&#123;chroot,iso/&#123;boot,isolinux,live&#125;&#125;
cd ~/mydistro</code></pre>
    <Note>
      <strong>Tip:</strong> Track your configuration files with Git from the start.
    </Note>
  </section>

  <section id="base-system">
    <h2>Base system</h2>
    <p>Use <code>debootstrap</code> to install a minimal Debian base into a chroot directory.</p>

    <h3>Step 1: Bootstrap the base</h3>
    <pre><code>sudo debootstrap --arch=amd64 --variant=minbase bullseye \
  ~/mydistro/chroot http://deb.debian.org/debian/</code></pre>
    <p>
      Replace <code>bullseye</code> with <code>bookworm</code> for Debian 12 or any other
      supported release codename.
    </p>

    <h3>Step 2: Mount system directories</h3>
    <pre><code>sudo mount --bind /dev     ~/mydistro/chroot/dev
sudo mount --bind /dev/pts ~/mydistro/chroot/dev/pts
sudo mount --bind /proc    ~/mydistro/chroot/proc
sudo mount --bind /sys     ~/mydistro/chroot/sys</code></pre>

    <h3>Step 3: Enter the chroot</h3>
    <pre><code>sudo chroot ~/mydistro/chroot /bin/bash</code></pre>

    <h3>Configure the base system</h3>
    <p>Run inside the chroot:</p>
    <pre><code>echo "mydistro" &gt; /etc/hostname

cat &gt; /etc/apt/sources.list &lt;&lt; EOF
deb http://deb.debian.org/debian bullseye main contrib non-free
deb http://deb.debian.org/debian-security bullseye-security main contrib non-free
deb http://deb.debian.org/debian bullseye-updates main contrib non-free
EOF

apt update
apt upgrade -y

apt install -y locales tzdata
dpkg-reconfigure locales
dpkg-reconfigure tzdata

apt install -y linux-image-amd64 live-boot systemd-sysv</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section id="customization">
    <h2>Customization</h2>

    <h3>Install a desktop environment</h3>

    <h4>GNOME</h4>
    <pre><code>apt install -y gnome-core gdm3 firefox-esr NetworkManager</code></pre>

    <h4>KDE Plasma</h4>
    <pre><code>apt install -y kde-standard sddm firefox-esr NetworkManager</code></pre>

    <h4>XFCE</h4>
    <pre><code>apt install -y xfce4 xfce4-goodies lightdm firefox-esr network-manager</code></pre>

    <h4>Minimal (Openbox)</h4>
    <pre><code>apt install -y xorg openbox lightdm tint2 nitrogen firefox-esr network-manager</code></pre>

    <h3>Install additional software</h3>
    <pre><code># Core utilities
apt install -y sudo nano vim-tiny less file htop gdebi gparted \
  synaptic apt-utils

# Multimedia and office
apt install -y vlc gimp libreoffice-writer libreoffice-calc

# Developer tools (optional)
apt install -y git build-essential</code></pre>

    <h3>Create the default user</h3>
    <pre><code>adduser liveuser
usermod -aG sudo liveuser

mkdir -p /etc/systemd/system/getty@tty1.service.d/
cat &gt; /etc/systemd/system/getty@tty1.service.d/override.conf &lt;&lt; EOF
[Service]
ExecStart=
ExecStart=-/sbin/agetty --autologin liveuser --noclear %I \$TERM
EOF</code></pre>
    <Warning>
      <strong>Warning:</strong> Autologin should only be used in the live environment. Never
      enable it in an installed system.
    </Warning>
  </section>

  <section id="package-management">
    <h2>Package management</h2>

    <h3>Create a custom repository (optional)</h3>
    <pre><code>apt install -y reprepro gpg

mkdir -p /var/www/repos/apt/debian
cd /var/www/repos/apt/debian

gpg --gen-key
gpg --export -a "Your Name" &gt; mydistro-key.asc</code></pre>

    <h3>Include packages from third-party sources</h3>
    <pre><code>wget -qO- https://packages.microsoft.com/keys/microsoft.asc \
  | gpg --dearmor &gt; microsoft.gpg
mv microsoft.gpg /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/microsoft.gpg
echo "deb [arch=amd64] https://packages.microsoft.com/repos/vscode stable main" \
  &gt; /etc/apt/sources.list.d/vscode.list

apt update
apt install -y code</code></pre>

    <h3>Create a meta-package</h3>
    <pre><code>apt install -y equivs
mkdir -p /tmp/metapackage
cd /tmp/metapackage
equivs-control mydistro-desktop.control</code></pre>

    <p>Example <code>mydistro-desktop.control</code>:</p>
    <pre><code>Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Standards-Version: 3.9.2
Package: mydistro-desktop
Version: 1.0
Maintainer: Your Name &lt;you@example.com&gt;
Depends: firefox-esr, libreoffice-writer, libreoffice-calc, vlc, gimp
Description: MyDistro desktop meta-package
 Installs all standard components for the MyDistro desktop environment.</code></pre>

    <pre><code>equivs-build mydistro-desktop.control
dpkg -i mydistro-desktop_1.0_all.deb
apt install -f</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section id="branding">
    <h2>Branding</h2>

    <h3>Custom GTK theme</h3>
    <pre><code>apt install -y gtk2-engines-murrine gtk2-engines-pixbuf
mkdir -p /usr/share/themes/MyDistro</code></pre>

    <h3>Plymouth boot screen</h3>
    <pre><code>apt install -y plymouth plymouth-themes
mkdir -p /usr/share/plymouth/themes/mydistro

cat &gt; /usr/share/plymouth/themes/mydistro/mydistro.plymouth &lt;&lt; EOF
[Plymouth Theme]
Name=MyDistro
Description=MyDistro Boot Screen
ModuleName=script

[script]
ImageDir=/usr/share/plymouth/themes/mydistro
ScriptFile=/usr/share/plymouth/themes/mydistro/mydistro.script
EOF

cat &gt; /usr/share/plymouth/themes/mydistro/mydistro.script &lt;&lt; EOF
Window.SetBackgroundTopColor(0.0, 0.0, 0.0);
Window.SetBackgroundBottomColor(0.0, 0.0, 0.0);

logo.image = Image("logo.png");
logo.sprite = Sprite(logo.image);
logo.sprite.SetX(Window.GetWidth() / 2 - logo.image.GetWidth() / 2);
logo.sprite.SetY(Window.GetHeight() / 2 - logo.image.GetHeight() / 2);
EOF

plymouth-set-default-theme -R mydistro</code></pre>
    <Note>
      <strong>Note:</strong> Place <code>logo.png</code> inside the theme directory before
      rebuilding the initramfs.
    </Note>

    <h3>Default wallpaper</h3>
    <pre><code>mkdir -p /usr/share/backgrounds/mydistro
cp /path/to/wallpaper.jpg /usr/share/backgrounds/mydistro/</code></pre>

    <h4>GNOME</h4>
    <pre><code>apt install -y dconf-cli
mkdir -p /etc/skel/.config/dconf
cat &gt; /etc/skel/.config/dconf/user.d/background.conf &lt;&lt; EOF
[org/gnome/desktop/background]
picture-uri='file:///usr/share/backgrounds/mydistro/wallpaper.jpg'
picture-options='stretched'
EOF</code></pre>

    <h4>KDE Plasma</h4>
    <pre><code>mkdir -p /etc/skel/.config/plasma-org.kde.plasma.desktop-appletsrc
cat &gt; /etc/skel/.config/plasma-org.kde.plasma.desktop-appletsrc &lt;&lt; EOF
[Containments][1][Wallpaper][org.kde.image][General]
Image=file:///usr/share/backgrounds/mydistro/wallpaper.jpg
EOF</code></pre>

    <h4>XFCE</h4>
    <pre><code>mkdir -p /etc/skel/.config/xfce4/xfconf/xfce-perchannel-xml
cat &gt; /etc/skel/.config/xfce4/xfconf/xfce-perchannel-xml/xfce4-desktop.xml &lt;&lt; EOF
&lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?&gt;
&lt;channel name="xfce4-desktop" version="1.0"&gt;
  &lt;property name="backdrop" type="empty"&gt;
    &lt;property name="screen0" type="empty"&gt;
      &lt;property name="monitor0" type="empty"&gt;
        &lt;property name="image-path" type="string"
                  value="/usr/share/backgrounds/mydistro/wallpaper.jpg"/&gt;
        &lt;property name="image-style" type="int" value="5"/&gt;
      &lt;/property&gt;
    &lt;/property&gt;
  &lt;/property&gt;
&lt;/channel&gt;
EOF</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section id="iso-creation">
    <h2>Building the ISO</h2>

    <h3>Clean up the chroot</h3>
    <pre><code>apt clean
rm -rf /tmp/*
exit</code></pre>

    <h3>Unmount and compress</h3>
    <pre><code>sudo umount ~/mydistro/chroot/dev/pts
sudo umount ~/mydistro/chroot/dev
sudo umount ~/mydistro/chroot/proc
sudo umount ~/mydistro/chroot/sys

sudo mksquashfs ~/mydistro/chroot ~/mydistro/iso/live/filesystem.squashfs \
  -comp xz -e boot</code></pre>

    <h3>Configure the bootloader</h3>
    <pre><code>sudo cp ~/mydistro/chroot/boot/vmlinuz-* ~/mydistro/iso/boot/vmlinuz
sudo cp ~/mydistro/chroot/boot/initrd.img-* ~/mydistro/iso/boot/initrd

sudo cp /usr/lib/ISOLINUX/isolinux.bin ~/mydistro/iso/isolinux/
sudo cp /usr/lib/syslinux/modules/bios/*.c32 ~/mydistro/iso/isolinux/

cat &gt; ~/mydistro/iso/isolinux/isolinux.cfg &lt;&lt; EOF
UI menu.c32
PROMPT 0
TIMEOUT 30
DEFAULT mydistro

LABEL mydistro
  MENU LABEL Start MyDistro
  LINUX /boot/vmlinuz
  INITRD /boot/initrd
  APPEND boot=live components quiet splash

LABEL mydistro_safe
  MENU LABEL Start MyDistro (Safe Graphics)
  LINUX /boot/vmlinuz
  INITRD /boot/initrd
  APPEND boot=live components quiet splash nomodeset
EOF</code></pre>

    <h3>Generate the ISO</h3>
    <pre><code>sudo xorriso -as mkisofs -r \
  -J -joliet-long -l -iso-level 3 \
  -partition_offset 16 \
  -publisher "MyDistro" \
  -A "MyDistro Live" \
  -b isolinux/isolinux.bin \
  -c isolinux/boot.cat \
  -no-emul-boot -boot-load-size 4 -boot-info-table \
  -o ~/mydistro.iso \
  ~/mydistro/iso/</code></pre>
    <Note>
      <strong>Note:</strong> Test the ISO in a VM before distributing it publicly.
    </Note>
  </section>

  <section id="testing">
    <h2>Testing</h2>

    <h3>Basic testing checklist</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>System boots successfully</li>
      <li>Network connectivity works</li>
      <li>Desktop environment launches</li>
      <li>Installed applications run correctly</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Extended testing checklist</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>System update (<code>apt upgrade</code>) succeeds</li>
      <li>Installing additional packages works</li>
      <li>Hardware compatibility (audio, webcam, Wi-Fi)</li>
      <li>Localization and input methods</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Test in QEMU</h3>
    <pre><code>qemu-system-x86_64 -boot d -cdrom ~/mydistro.iso -m 2048</code></pre>
    <Warning>
      <strong>Warning:</strong> Always test both in live mode and after installation to disk
      before a public release.
    </Warning>
  </section>

  <section id="distribution">
    <h2>Distribution</h2>

    <h3>Generate checksums</h3>
    <pre><code>cd ~/
md5sum mydistro.iso &gt; mydistro.iso.md5
sha256sum mydistro.iso &gt; mydistro.iso.sha256</code></pre>

    <h3>Release checklist</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Write release notes / changelog</li>
      <li>Verify licenses of all included components</li>
      <li>Set up a website and bug tracker</li>
      <li>Publish ISO and checksums to a reliable hosting provider</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Ongoing maintenance</h3>
    <p>
      After the first release you need to keep your distribution up to date with Debian security
      patches, rebuild the ISO periodically, and triage user-reported bugs. Consider setting up
      automatic rebuild pipelines with CI tools like Jenkins or GitHub Actions.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuideLayout>
